'''arbitrarily''' (är′bi-trā-ri-li), ''adv.'' In an arbitrary manner; at will; capriciously; without sufficient reason; in an irresponsible or despotic way.
{{smaller block|The Bishop of Dunkeld, who . . . had opposed the government, was ''arbitrarily'' ejected from his see, and a successor was appointed.
{{right|''Macaulay'', Hist. Eng., vi.}}}}

'''arbitrariness''' (är′bi-trạ̄-ri-nes), ''n.'' The quality of being arbitrary.
{{smaller block|Consciousness is an entangled plexus which cannot be cut into parts without more or less ''arbitrariness.''
{{right|''H. Spencer'', Prin. of Psychol., § 480.}}}}

