{{smaller block|They perpetually sacrifice nature and reason to ''arbitrary'' canons of taste. {{right|''Macaulay'', Dryden.}}}}
{{smaller block|By an ''arbitrary'' proceeding, I mean one conducted by the private opinions or feelings of the man who attempts to regulate. {{right|''Burke.''}}}}
